		code: "def forward(self, x, y):\n    add = torch.sub(x, y);  y = None\n    mul = torch.mul(add, 2);  add = None\n    sin = torch.sin(x);  x = sin = None\n    relu = torch.relu(mul);  mul = None\n    return relu\n",
		marks: [
			[1, "swap"],
			[3, "dce"],
		],
		note: "Changing node.target swaps the function the node calls; the node keeps its name, add. Output: [1.0, 0.0, 8.0].",
